{"id": "EUVD-2026-90258", "enisaUuid": "698d7db5-f9b5-3398-ac3a-04075f819d9d", "description": "ZeroClaw versions before 0.8.5 built with plugins-wasm feature contain a path traversal vulnerability in plugin installation that fails to validate the wasm_path manifest field. Attackers can convince users to install crafted plugins that write arbitrary files to paths outside the plugins directory, such as shell startup files, enabling code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-09-30T19:16:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T19:55:05", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/security/advisories/GHSA-93f6-34w8-5g98", "https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/commit/432e034d3cb024610d5916a2f328678d151c1dd5", "https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/releases/tag/v0.8.5", "https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/blob/v0.8.4/crates/zeroclaw-plugins/src/host.rs#L238-L273", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zeroclaw-before-0.8.5-path-traversal-via-plugin-manifest-wasm-path"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-101885", "GHSA-7wjp-5q22-qfc3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6d99de90-ef4b-3d79-8773-aee069ba37d0", "product": {"name": "ZeroClaw", "vendor": {"name": "zeroclaw-labs"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.8.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7bd85149-92d7-3c36-83be-e7be53089b19", "vendor": {"name": "zeroclaw-labs"}}], "isExploited": false}